# Structures and what they implement

[elab](README.md)

Every public structure of the library that says which signature it implements. A structure is
documented on the page of its signature. `:>` means that the source seals the structure with the
signature; `:` that it matches it, which the test suite checks.

| Structure | Signature | Realisations | Status |  | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Box` | : [`BOX`](sig/BOX.md) | `where type elem = int` | required | an application of `RuneBoxFn` | [tests/doc/elab.lib/box.sml](../../../../tests/doc/elab.lib/box.sml) |
| `Chest` | : [`BOX`](sig/BOX.md) | `where type elem = string` | required |  | [tests/doc/elab.lib/box.sml](../../../../tests/doc/elab.lib/box.sml) |
| `Crate` | : [`BOX`](sig/BOX.md) | `where type elem = int` | required | is `Box` | [tests/doc/elab.lib/box.sml](../../../../tests/doc/elab.lib/box.sml) |

## Names beyond the signature

What a structure declares and its signatures do not specify. Most structures are not sealed, so
these names are visible; a program that uses them is not portable. A structure that is another
one by name has the names of that one, and an application of a functor those of the functor's body.

| Structure | Also declares |
| --- | --- |
| `Box` | `full` |
| `Chest` | `spare` |
| `Crate` | `full` |

